<aside class="quick-answer not-prose" aria-labelledby="quick-answer-title">
  <p id="quick-answer-title" class="quick-answer-label">Quick answer</p>
  <p><strong>No, Apple Watch cannot measure or track cortisol.</strong> It has no cortisol sensor and shows no cortisol level.</p>
  <p>It records heart rate, heart rate variability (HRV) and sleep. Apps such as Cortisol+ turn those signals into a wellness score, not a hormone reading. Only a <a href="https://medlineplus.gov/lab-tests/cortisol-test/">blood, saliva or urine test</a> measures cortisol.</p>
</aside>

